Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "FloodedUrbanPedestrianScenario" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3, :risk4 ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 .

:actor1 a :Pedestrian ;
    :description "Pedestrian walking in flooded street" .

:weather1 a :RainyCondition ;
    :description "Heavy rain causing flooding" .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Floodwater covering road surface" .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Pedestrian walking in flooded roadway with potential vehicle collision" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Slippery and flooded road conditions" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Reduced visibility due to heavy rain and flooding" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:risk4 a :DistractionRisk ;
    :description "Driver distraction due to unusual flooding in urban area" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev4 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.92"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.88"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.85"^^xsd:float .

:sev4 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Pedestrian walking in flooded roadway with potential vehicle collision
Severity Score: 0.92

**Risk 2:**
Description: Slippery and flooded road conditions
Severity Score: 0.88

**Risk 3:**
Description: Reduced visibility due to heavy rain and flooding
Severity Score: 0.85

**Risk 4:**
Description: Driver distraction due to unusual flooding in urban area
Severity Score: 0.75

The corner case is classified as a **StateAnomaly** because the primary issue stems from the unusual state of the environment (flooded roadway) rather than an anomalous behavior or evidence-based anomaly. The pedestrian is simply navigating through an unexpected condition.